Risk to test: R1 P2 "Auto-commit with work handed to a thread pool" at PaymentListener#onMessage, where the outcome would be: lost. In PaymentListener.java at line 37, the code submits the message processing task to a thread pool and immediately calls ack.acknowledge() on the main listener thread. If the application crashes after acknowledgement but before the background task completes, the offset is lost and data is dropped.

The fault: Faultline will crash worker-1 the moment PaymentListener#onMessage returns, on every 150th message, 2 times: what it handed off is still running. The checks it already makes: no-lost, no-duplicates, no-unexpected, faults-fired.

