## HTTP endpoints that take a request body

- POST /payments -> PaymentController#pay

## Their request bodies

### POST /payments (from PaymentRequested)

- paymentId: string
- accountId: string
- amountMinor: integer, required

## Their handlers and request types

```java
@RestController
class PaymentController {

    private final KafkaTemplate<String, String> kafka;

    private final JsonMapper json;

    private final String topic;

    PaymentController(KafkaTemplate<String, String> kafka, JsonMapper json, @Value("${payments.inbound-topic:payments.requested}") String topic) {
        this.kafka = kafka;
        this.json = json;
        this.topic = topic;
    }

    @PostMapping("/payments")
    ResponseEntity<Void> pay(@RequestBody PaymentRequested req) throws Exception {
        var event = new PaymentEvent(UUID.randomUUID().toString(), req.paymentId(), req.accountId(), req.amountMinor());
        kafka.send(topic, req.accountId(), json.writeValueAsString(event)).get();
        return ResponseEntity.accepted().build();
    }
}

public record PaymentRequested(String paymentId, String accountId, long amountMinor) {
}
